'''''Wimmeria''''' is a [[genus]] of [[shrub]]s to small [[tree]]s in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Celastraceae]].<ref>Shreve & Wiggins, p. 849</ref> It includes 17 species native to Mexico and Central America.<ref name = powo>{{cite web |title=''Wimmeria'' Schltdl. & Cham. |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:6709-1 |website=[[Plants of the World Online]] |publisher=[[Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew]] |access-date=1 April 2026}}</ref> It is named after German [[botanist]] [[Christian Friedrich Heinrich Wimmer]] (1803–1868).

==Species==
17 species are accepted.<ref name = powo/>
